Build the recorder with optimisation. The rule has never had any.

    rx_uhd_ext_gps: rx_uhd_ext_gps.cpp
    	g++ -std=c++11 `pkg-config --cflags ...` -o rx_uhd_ext_gps ...

No `-O` flag anywhere, which means **`-O0`**: no inlining, every local spilled
to the stack, no vectorisation. That is a debug build, and this program moves
100 MB/s off a USRP against a hard deadline.

It is not the cause of DOB's packet loss -- an `-O2` rebuild on 2026-08-11
moved the drop rate from 52% to 42%, i.e. nowhere, and the real cause was CPU
contention (`docs/2026-08-11-recorder-packet-loss.md` §2). This patch is here
for a duller reason: **the fix does not survive `make`.**

DOB is currently running an optimised binary built by hand:

    g++ -O2 -std=c++11 $(pkg-config --cflags uhd hdf5 digital_rf) \
        -o rx_uhd_ext_gps rx_uhd_ext_gps.cpp -pthread ...

The next person to follow `patches/README.md`'s instruction -- `make
rx_uhd_ext_gps`, which is what applying patch 0001 tells you to do -- silently
replaces it with an `-O0` build. Nothing warns. The binary compiles, starts,
locks the GPSDO and records; it is simply slower, and on a machine that is
already contended that matters at exactly the wrong moment.

`-O2`, not `-O3` or `-march=native`. `-O2` is the boring, portable choice, and
the binary is copied between machines by `scp` often enough that baking in the
host's instruction set would be a trap of its own. If you want more, measure it
-- and measure it against the drop counters, not a stopwatch.

Only `rx_uhd_ext_gps` is changed. `rx_uhd` and `libdownconvert.so` have the
same omission and could take the same flag, but neither has a deadline, and a
patch that edits three rules is a patch that fails to apply for three reasons.

    cd ~/chirpsounder2
    git apply --check /path/to/0006-makefile-build-recorder-with-O2.patch
    git apply         /path/to/0006-makefile-build-recorder-with-O2.patch
    make rx_uhd_ext_gps
    sudo setcap cap_sys_nice+ep rx_uhd_ext_gps    # inode changed; caps are gone

That last line is not optional. `setcap` attaches to the inode, so every
rebuild drops it, and under `dombas.sh` there is no `LimitRTPRIO` to make up
for it.

Verify the flag actually reached the compiler rather than trusting the diff:

    make -n rx_uhd_ext_gps | grep -o '\-O[0-9s]*'

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -12,2 +12,2 @@ rx_uhd_ext_gps: rx_uhd_ext_gps.cpp
 rx_uhd_ext_gps: rx_uhd_ext_gps.cpp
-	g++ -std=c++11 `pkg-config --cflags uhd hdf5 digital_rf` -o rx_uhd_ext_gps rx_uhd_ext_gps.cpp -pthread  -lboost_program_options -lboost_system -lboost_thread -lboost_date_time -lboost_regex -lboost_serialization -ldigital_rf `pkg-config --libs uhd hdf5 digital_rf`
+	g++ -O2 -std=c++11 `pkg-config --cflags uhd hdf5 digital_rf` -o rx_uhd_ext_gps rx_uhd_ext_gps.cpp -pthread  -lboost_program_options -lboost_system -lboost_thread -lboost_date_time -lboost_regex -lboost_serialization -ldigital_rf `pkg-config --libs uhd hdf5 digital_rf`
